{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJVTJiFYYomuSt2pXP5F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A prudent agent exists at modal depth 2, and no agent of depth 0 or 1 can be prudent. I've written both to `/work/answer.md`, written `/work/SUBMIT`, and appended `[sonnet2] FINAL` to the board.\n\n**Agent.** The formula is `B(a & (B(F) | ~d))`. This is PrudentBot: it cooperates iff PA proves the opponent cooperates with it and PA+Con(PA) proves the opponent defects against DefectBot. `check.py` reports it as prudent:\n\n| opponent | action |\n|---|---|\n| CooperateBot | D |\n| DefectBot | D |\n| FairBot | C (FairBot replies C) |\n| itself | C |\n\n**Lower bound.** A depth-0 or depth-1 formula is a Boolean combination of boxes over Boolean functions of a, c and d. The argument has three steps:\n- **Against CooperateBot:** a, c and d are all true at every world, so the action is constant from world 1 on. Prudence requires that constant to be D.\n- **Against FairBot at world 1:** only world 0 lies below, and there all three atoms are true (FairBot's □ is vacuous at world 0). That is the same input as against CooperateBot, so the agent plays D at world 1.\n- **FairBot's reply:** FairBot then defects against the agent from world 2 on, so FairBot's stable reply is D, but prudence requires C.\n\nThis holds for any formula size, with no enumeration.\n\n**Unfinished.** I did not characterize the depth-2 prudent agents or bound their minimal size. The only size remark is that the problem's search (no constants, up to 7 symbols) found none, so a constant-free prudent agent needs more than 7 symbols. My formula uses the constant `F`.\n\nI never saw any board entries from `sonnet` before submitting, so my answer was not reviewed or agreed with them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":238